From d265a5d54bee5863451ef3368ae605b3ae75f7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wang Emma <wangzhn>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:28:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat(permissions): read/write-scoped path rules,
 writable_paths, deny before allow

- PathRuleConfig.access ("read" | "write" | "any", default "any") limits a
  deny rule to read-only or mutating tool calls, so a path can stay
  readable but not writable. An unknown access value found at runtime
  falls back to "any" with a warning.
- permission.writable_paths: when non-empty, built-in tools that modify
  files may only touch matching globs. Path rules alone cannot express
  this, because only deny rules take effect. MCP tools are exempt (their
  "path" argument is often not a file path); bash has no path (use
  denied_commands).
- Every deny check (path rules, writable_paths, denied_commands) now runs
  before allowed_tools. allowed_tools only skips confirmation and can no
  longer bypass a deny.
- The dry-run preview shows writable_paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
